  "body": "v1.12.2\r\n\r\nCode tab\r\n\r\n- Long diff lines can wrap instead of scrolling sideways: a scroll /\r\n  wrap pair at the end of the Diff / Commits row switches every diff,\r\n  and the choice is remembered (S7NVYBN, #434)\r\n\r\nHeadless and behind a proxy\r\n\r\n- `epiq gui` no longer exits when no browser opener is installed; it\r\n  keeps serving and prints the URL (KRJD9HJ, #429)\r\n- `epiq gui --no-open` serves without opening a browser, and on Linux\r\n  with no display it skips the open on its own (KRJD9HJ, #429)\r\n- The board connects over wss:// when the GUI is served over https, so\r\n  it no longer loads blank behind a TLS-terminating proxy (5YXJATQ,\r\n  #429)\r\n\r\nFixes\r\n\r\n- Switching tab on a ticket keeps the board's zoomed window; a diff\r\n  link's line range had been clearing it (TGPKA5V)\r\n- The Code series' line bars are scaled against the largest bucket on a\r\n  log scale, so busy periods no longer clip to one height (KSMVDM8)"
